{
  "_comment": [
    "Wiring for the awareness layer. Merge into your harness's settings file.",
    "See _AWARENESS.md for what each register is and why none of these block.",
    "",
    "Event names below are the common ones. CONFIRM AGAINST YOUR HARNESS'S HOOK",
    "DOCUMENTATION before relying on any of it — what a hook may return, and",
    "whether its stdout reaches the model, differs per event and per harness.",
    "Phase 9 exists because assumptions about the environment are where plans die.",
    "",
    "Start with the PreCompact + SessionStart PAIR — they are one system, not a",
    "ranking. Inject before the boundary so the summary can keep the frame; re-establish",
    "after it because measurably, half the time, the summary did not. In the first pilot",
    "the post-boundary register held the frame 3/3; verbatim survival into the summary",
    "was 1/2. Add the rest once you have seen the pair work.",
    "",
    "AWARENESS points at your copy of awareness.sh. Use an absolute path or a",
    "variable your harness expands — a relative path resolves against whatever",
    "directory the hook happens to run in, which is not a promise you have."
  ],

  "hooks": {

    "PreCompact": [
      {
        "_why": "Fires immediately before the context is summarised, so the frame has a chance to land INSIDE the summary. Measured 1/2 for verbatim survival — pair it with SessionStart, which re-fires after the boundary and held 3/3.",
        "matcher": "*",
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "bash \"$AWARENESS\" precompact", "timeout": 10 }
        ]
      }
    ],

    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "_why": "Cold or warm start — AND it re-fires on the post-compact context, which is the measured backstop when the summariser drops the injected frame. Never resume by starting at task 1.",
        "matcher": "*",
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "bash \"$AWARENESS\" checkpoint", "timeout": 10 }
        ]
      }
    ],

    "SubagentStop": [
      {
        "_why": "A worker finished: one unit closed, the cheapest moment to zoom out. This is the wave boundary.",
        "matcher": "*",
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "bash \"$AWARENESS\" checkpoint", "timeout": 10 }
        ]
      }
    ],

    "PostToolUse": [
      {
        "_why": "SILENT. A status line was written — the only work-shaped event a harness offers. Refreshes the requester's surface. Prints nothing: this register's audience is not the agent.",
        "_note": "Narrow the matcher to your task-file path so this fires on work boundaries, not on every write.",
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "bash \"$AWARENESS\" record", "timeout": 10 }
        ]
      }
    ],

    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "_why": "Situational, and NON-BLOCKING by design. Notes that a file has an owner; never denies. Enforcement belongs in _RULES.md, not here.",
        "_note": "Requires an OWNERS file — the phase-7 contended-file list. Without one this is a no-op, which is the correct failure.",
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "bash \"$AWARENESS\" situational \"$CLAUDE_TOOL_FILE_PATH\"", "timeout": 5 }
        ]
      }
    ],

    "Stop": [
      {
        "_why": "Turn ended. Asks whether the status line reflects what just happened — the check that keeps principle 13 self-maintaining rather than aspirational.",
        "matcher": "*",
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "bash \"$AWARENESS\" stale", "timeout": 5 }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },

  "_deliberately_absent": {
    "UserPromptSubmit": [
      "The ambient register — one line, every turn — is the one most likely to become noise,",
      "and noise is expensive here: an agent that learns injected text is skippable stops",
      "reading the reminders that matter. Add it only once the punctuated ones have proved",
      "useful, and only if you actually miss it."
    ]
  },

  "_before_you_add_more": [
    "Every reminder competes for the same attention. Adding one makes the others",
    "cheaper to ignore. The test for a new hook is not 'does this moment exist' but",
    "'does a worker at this moment need something it does not have'."
  ]
}
